KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ rethrown: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
no body for callee
--
std::current_exception, std::rethrow_exception and exception_ptr's
_M_addref/_M_release are defined in libstdc++'s compiled library.  They now
have models (cpp_typecheck_stdlib.cpp) whose intrinsics remove_cpp_exceptions
lowers: the exception object of a handler, its number of exception_ptrs, and
a rethrow that makes it the in-flight exception with its type tag.
